    "result_text": "You can now mark a charge line as tax-free, but **tax is still worked out on those lines for now.** The acceptance spec says that the calculation that leaves them out is a later checkpoint, so I added only the flag and its marker. Until that change lands, ticking the box doesn't change the invoice total. `bin/e2e` passes.\n\n**What's in it:**\n- **Database:** `V32__line_item_tax_exempt.sql` adds a `tax_exempt` column to line items. It defaults to false, so existing lines stay taxable.\n- **Server:** The server is Spring Boot; \"OfficeFloor\" is only the package name. Line items now store `taxExempt` and return it in API responses. Adding or editing a line accepts it too, and a line that doesn't say is taxable. The test seeding endpoint also accepts `taxExempt` on seeded lines.\n- **Front end** (`invoice-detail.ts`):\n  - Tax-free lines show \"(tax-free)\" next to the description (`lineitem-taxexempt`).\n  - The add-line form has a labelled \"Tax-free\" checkbox (`lineitem-form-taxexempt`).\n  - Editing a line in place also has the checkbox (`lineitem-edit-taxexempt`), so saving an edit keeps the flag instead of resetting it.\n\n**One `data-testid` moved:** to fit the marker in the description cell, `lineitem-description` is now on a `<span>` inside the cell rather than on the cell itself. The name and its text are the same, but it now sits on a different element.",
